# Line-ending policy. Everything checks out as LF on every platform, so a
# Windows clone cannot rewrite text files to CRLF. This repository depends on
# exact bytes more than most: a certificate is bound to the hash of the
# original problem file, the tamper corpus and hand-worked verifier vectors are
# compared verbatim, and the determinism gate compares two runs of the same
# trace with `cmp`. A CRLF rewrite breaks those comparisons for a reason that
# is slow to diagnose.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Instance and certificate fixtures are hashed as-is. Never normalize them.
*.mps -text
*.lp -text
*.hcc -text

# Binary — never convert
*.gif binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
*.wasm binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
